{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "John in Argentina"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "A Music Festival"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 17}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Identifies general information in short written and spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Identifies general information in short written and spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Identifies general information in short written and spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Identifies general information in short written and spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Identifies general information in short written and spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Identifies general information in short written and spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Identifies general information in short written and spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Identifies general information in short written and spoken conversations."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Simple Present vs. The Present Continuous"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "example", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Simple Present tense to talk about:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul>  \t<li>a routine action or specific action that happens regularly </li> \t<li>a general truth </li> \t<li>personal information </li>  </ul>   \t\t\t"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use expressions of frequency like <span class=\"italic\">every day</span> or <span class=\"italic\">always</span> with the Present Simple."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Present Continuous tense to talk about:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul>  \t<li>a current event or an action happening around now   </li> \t<li>events that <span class =\"strong\">are happening</span> soon (future plans) </li></ul>   \t\t\t"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You form the Present Continuous with the verb <span class =\"strong\">to be + verb-ing</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use expressions like <span class=\"italic\">right now</span> or <span class=\"italic\">later</span> with the Present Continuous."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Every April, artists, musicians and chefs <span class=\"strong\">come</span> together to create an artistic theme park. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You guys <span class =\"strong\">are planning</span> another trip to Argentina, now?"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "theme park "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an amusement park with a common setting or idea "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Every April, artists come together to create a theme park."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le17ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about a festival."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Hold on\u2026 "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "wait for a moment "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Hold on...I'm checking the map."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le17ob05aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sector "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "area; district "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Examp